From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] console: carry the pre-relocation record over to the relocated buffer

With CONSOLE_RECORD_INIT_F the console is recorded from before relocation,
into a small buffer in the early malloc area.  console_record_init() then
runs a second time from board_init_r() and simply allocates a fresh buffer,
so everything recorded so far -- the banner, the CPU line, the DRAM size --
is dropped on the floor.

Copy the early buffer's contents into the new one before recording goes on.
The early buffer sits in the pre-relocation malloc area, which nothing has
touched this early in board_init_r().

The web recovery server's GET /log (202) serves this record to a user who
has no serial adapter; without this hunk the first thing they would see is
"Core:", with the DRAM size gone.

diff --git a/common/console.c b/common/console.c
--- a/common/console.c
+++ b/common/console.c
@@ -835,6 +835,7 @@ void flush(void)
 #ifdef CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD
 int console_record_init(void)
 {
+	struct membuf early = *(struct membuf *)&gd->console_out;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = membuf_new((struct membuf *)&gd->console_out,
@@ -843,6 +844,30 @@ int console_record_init(void)
 				CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD_OUT_SIZE_F);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Called a second time after relocation: carry over what the
+	 * pre-relocation buffer holds (the banner, CPU and DRAM lines), so a
+	 * reader of the record sees the boot from the top rather than from
+	 * board_init_r().  The early buffer lives in the pre-relocation
+	 * malloc area, which is still intact this early in board_init_r().
+	 */
+	if ((gd->flags & GD_FLG_RELOC) && early.start) {
+		char *data;
+		int len, i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+			len = membuf_getraw(&early, -1, true, &data);
+			if (len <= 0)
+				break;
+			membuf_put((struct membuf *)&gd->console_out, data, len);
+		}
+		/*
+		 * An overflow of the early buffer was that buffer's; the
+		 * flag would otherwise tell a reader that this one is full.
+		 */
+		gd->flags &= ~GD_FLG_RECORD_OVF;
+	}
 	ret = membuf_new((struct membuf *)&gd->console_in,
 			 CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD_IN_SIZE);
 
